From 93f0896b446d08242cc6edad530459a65f37c60f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Agnya <manthram@Pradass-MacBook-Pro.local>
Date: Wed, 9 Sep 2026 22:53:25 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] Fix remaining old-brand-green color bugs (emerald wasn't in
 earlier searches)

Found while chasing a leftover green tint on the Calendar page title: my
earlier color-audit passes searched for "green-" and "blue-" but not
"emerald-", which is the specific Tailwind shade several old-brand
elements were hardcoded to. That let a real one slip through, so I did a
proper sweep this time.

Fixed (all single-accent "this is the app's identity color" moments,
same category as the earlier header bugs):
- navigation.tsx: the authenticated nav bar background was hardcoded to
  the literal old hex (#1E7A50/#165c3c), not even the ceylon-green alias
  -- meaning every logged-in user has been seeing the old dark-green nav
  bar this whole rebrand. Also fixed ~14 text-emerald-100 hover states
  (designed for that green background) and the mobile menu panel.
- Calendar's second "Calendar" section title (missed the first pass --
  only the day-preview panel header got fixed then).
- TipsBox.tsx (the "Pro Tips" boxes on Browse Trips and Calendar).
- chat-buddy.tsx: page header, message-send button, and the sent-message
  bubble color.
- PreferencesForm.tsx: only the two generic "add option" affordances
  reused across all sections, not the section headers themselves.

Deliberately NOT changed: PreferencesForm's six section headers (each a
different pastel color on purpose, for wayfinding in a long form), the
three profile stat cards (same reasoning), and question-detail's
accepted-answer highlight (a real status semantic, not a brand color).
Consistent with leaving the per-province badge colors and Quick Trip
urgency styling alone in the earlier pass.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
